# Complete the source-faithful world before player and vehicle polish

Build the complete playable world before final character or vehicle assets.
World correctness includes exterior levels, interiors, props, authored
placement,
collision, locators, streaming ownership, and traversal continuity.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Publish all source-backed exterior levels and interiors into the playable
  Unreal world without manual placement fixes.
- [ ] Preserve authored props, collision, locators, world transforms, and
  streaming relationships needed by gameplay.
- [ ] Make the world traversable with representative runtime actors before
  requiring final player or vehicle presentation.
- [ ] Treat final materials, character art, vehicle art, and animation polish as
  later work unless a minimum representation is required for world behavior.

## Dependencies

Depends on the Unreal runtime foundation.
